# Kortex — Cursor / Antigravity rules

Match existing Antigravity patterns. Prefer the smallest change that works. Do not invent new architecture without an explicit ask.

## Tech stack

Monorepo (`kortex-monorepo`):

| Package | Stack |
|---------|--------|
| `frontend/` | React 18, Vite, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Zustand, TanStack Query, `@hello-pangea/dnd`, Lucide, date-fns, sonner |
| `backend/` | Express, Prisma, Socket.io, TypeScript |
| `shared/` | `@kortex/shared` — types, roles, status categories, socket events |

Deploy: Vercel static frontend (offline demo falls back to mocks in `frontend/src/api/queries.ts` when API fails). Root `vercel.json` serves `frontend/dist`.

## Folder layout

```
frontend/src/
  api/           # client, queries (TanStack + mock fallbacks), socket
  components/
    layout/      # AppLayout, Sidebar, Header, ViewTabs
    views/       # List, Kanban, Backlog, Gantt, Calendar, Workload, MindMap, Table, Overview
    tasks/       # TaskDetailModal, TaskCreateModal, BulkActionBar
    search/      # CommandPalette
    common/      # Avatar, badges, ToastManager
    docs/ agile/ automations/ dashboards/ settings/ time/ auth/
  store/         # useAppStore, useAuthStore, usePresenceStore (Zustand)
  lib/           # helpers (sanitizeText, useFocusTrap, urlFilters, agentWorkflow)
  App.tsx

backend/src/
  routes/ controllers/ services/ middleware/ sockets/ db.ts server.ts

shared/src/      # shared types & constants
```

## Component patterns

- Functional components + TypeScript. Co-locate view-specific UI under `components/views/` or feature folders.
- Data: TanStack Query hooks in `api/queries.ts` (`useTasks`, `useProject`, mutations). Always keep offline/mock fallbacks working.
- UI state (project, view, filters, modals, theme, timer): Zustand `useAppStore`. Auth: `useAuthStore`.
- Task text is plain text only — use `sanitizePlainText` from `lib/sanitizeText.ts` on titles/descriptions/comments. Never `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` for user content.
- Modals/drawers: `role="dialog"`, `aria-modal`, Esc + focus trap via `useFocusTrap`.
- DnD: `@hello-pangea/dnd` on Kanban; when updating status, write the full `status` object as well as `statusId` (optimistic cache).

## Styling (Tailwind)

- Prefer CSS variables already defined for theme tokens: `var(--bg-*)`, `var(--text-*)`, `var(--border-*)`. Do not hardcode slate/indigo dark hex in new code when a token exists.
- Typography: rem root ~16px standard; avoid `text-[10px]` / `text-[11px]` — use `text-xs`+.
- Layout: `select-none` on board chrome; `break-words` / `line-clamp` on long titles; `min-w-0` in flex rows that truncate.
- Accent: indigo is the established product accent — stay consistent; do not introduce a new purple-gradient marketing look on app chrome.
- Motion: light `animate-in` / transition utilities only; no decorative glow stacks.

## State & URL

- Session nav (project/view/section/filters) → `localStorage` key `kortex_session_nav`.
- Offline mock task mutations → `kortex_mock_tasks` (merge new seed ids on load).
- List / Kanban / Spreadsheet filters also sync to the URL (`useUrlFilterSync` + `lib/urlFilters.ts`):  
  `?view=BOARD&search=auth&priority=HIGH&type=BUG&sprint=…&sort=priority&my=1`  
  URL wins on first load for bookmark/share.
- Sprint filter semantics: `filters.sprintId` — `undefined` = all, `null` = backlog, `string` = that sprint.
- Appearance: `kortex_theme`, `kortex_font`, `kortex_size`, `kortex_sizepx`, etc.

## Agent workflow (mandatory — Cursor & Antigravity)

Users: `cursor@kortex.dev` / `antigravity@kortex.dev` (password `password123`).

1. **Prompt → tasks first:** one DEV task per distinct ask, before code. Plain-language titles. Assign executor. Active sprint. Description cites originating request. Prefer linking an existing open/recent task (`findOverlappingAgentTask`) over duplicates.
2. **Live statuses:** To Do → In Progress → In Review → Deploying → Done, or **Blocked**. Board columns include Deploying / Blocked.
3. **No batching fixes:** one bug/feature = one task = one commit (`DEV-N: …`) = one deploy. Do not squash multiple fixes into one task.
4. **Docs in the same task:** update mock Docs — **Kortex Platform Walkthrough** + dated **Kortex Changelog** (and Platform Guide chapter when relevant). Mark partial features `🚧 Partial`.
5. **Helpers:** `frontend/src/lib/agentWorkflow.ts` (+ `*.check.ts` self-checks). Leave a minimal runnable check for non-trivial logic.
6. **End-of-prompt summary:**
   ```
   Tasks: DEV-N (status) · …
   Changed: …
   Docs: Walkthrough §… · Changelog …
   Deploy: <url|failed> · commit <sha>
   ```
7. Failed verify/deploy = Blocked, not Done. Broken prod → rollback + Blocked.

## Do / Don't

- **Do** fix bugs only when asked for QA — do not rebuild working features.
- **Do** keep mock data + offline demo path green (Vercel static).
- **Don't** start offline-first IndexedDB/Supabase sync without an explicit architectural decision.
- **Don't** add dependencies if stdlib / existing packages cover it.
- **Don't** create abstractions, new design systems, or drive-by refactors.
- **Don't** invent Calendar timelines as DnD boards — Timeline/Gantt currently has no card DnD; do not rebuild unless tasked.

## Commits & PRs

- Branch prefix: `cursor/<descriptive-name>-…`
- Commit message: `DEV-N: short imperative summary`
- Prefer feature branch + PR; temporary Vercel deploy of `frontend/dist` when auth is unavailable (`npx vercel deploy frontend/dist --temporary --yes`).
